# Ollama-OpenAI Proxy Project Architecture

This is the main **Ollama-OpenAI Proxy** project - a Go 1.25 application that provides OpenAI-compatible API for local Ollama models.

## 🏗️ Project Structure

### Entry Points
- [cmd/server/main.go](mdc:cmd/server/main.go) - HTTP server with OpenAI API endpoints
- [cmd/tui/main.go](mdc:cmd/tui/main.go) - Terminal UI for monitoring and management

### Core Configuration  
- [internal/config/config.go](mdc:internal/config/config.go) - Complete configuration system
- [configs/dev.yaml](mdc:configs/dev.yaml) - Development configuration
- [configs/production.yaml.example](mdc:configs/production.yaml.example) - Production template

### Architecture Layers
```
Client Apps (OpenAI API) → Proxy Server → Ollama Server
                            ↓
                    [API Keys & Auth] → [Models & Metrics]
                            ↓
                    [Terminal UI (TUI)]
```

## 🎯 Key Principles

### Go 1.25 Features
- Utilize **enhanced generics** where appropriate
- Use **improved WaitGroups** with proper error handling  
- Leverage **new vet analyzers** (`-waitgroup`, `-hostport`)
- Apply **memory leak detection** capabilities

### OpenAI Compatibility 
- **Exact API format** matching for `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/models`
- **Request/Response conversion** between OpenAI ↔ Ollama formats
- **Streaming support** for real-time responses
- **Error format consistency** with OpenAI standards

### Security First
- **API Key Management** with model-based access control
- **Rate Limiting** per API key with configurable limits
- **Audit Logging** for all authentication events
- **Secure storage** with bcrypt/argon2 hashing

### 100% Test Coverage
- Every component must have **comprehensive unit tests**
- **Integration tests** with mock Ollama server
- **Edge cases coverage** for all error scenarios
- **Performance benchmarks** for critical paths

## 🚀 CPU Cache-Friendly Data Structures

### КРИТИЧНО: Всегда проверяй на False Sharing

При создании структур с concurrent access:

#### ❌ ПЛОХО: Счетчики в одной cache line
```go
type Stats struct {
    TotalRequests   int64  // \
    ActiveRequests  int64  //  | Все в одной
    SuccessRequests int64  //  | 64-byte cache line
    ErrorRequests   int64  // /  → False sharing!
}
```

#### ✅ ХОРОШО: Cache line padding
```go
type Stats struct {
    TotalRequests int64
    _pad1         [56]byte  // 64 - 8 = 56 bytes padding
    
    ActiveRequests int64
    _pad2          [56]byte
    
    SuccessRequests int64
    _pad3           [56]byte
    
    ErrorRequests int64
    _pad4          [56]byte
}
```

### Когда использовать Cache Line Padding

✅ **ИСПОЛЬЗУЙ для:**
- Global counters с high contention (Stats, Metrics)
- Per-key atomic counters при >100 updates/sec
- Любые atomic variables обновляемые из множества goroutines
- Shared state между CPU cores

❌ **НЕ ИСПОЛЬЗУЙ для:**
- Редко обновляемых структур (User, Tenant, Configuration)
- Single-threaded операций
- Read-only data
- Структур с низкой contention (<10 updates/sec)

### Atomic Operations - ОБЯЗАТЕЛЬНО

#### ❌ ПЛОХО: Race condition
```go
type Counter struct {
    value int64  // НЕ thread-safe!
}

func (c *Counter) Increment() {
    c.value++  // Race condition!
}
```

#### ✅ ХОРОШО: Atomic operations
```go
type Counter struct {
    value int64
    _pad  [56]byte  // Padding если есть другие atomic fields
}

func (c *Counter) Increment() {
    atomic.AddInt64(&c.value, 1)  // Thread-safe
}

func (c *Counter) Get() int64 {
    return atomic.LoadInt64(&c.value)  // Thread-safe read
}
```

### Hot/Cold Data Splitting

#### ❌ ПЛОХО: Mixed hot/cold data
```go
type APIKey struct {
    // HOT - используется каждый запрос
    ID     string
    Status APIKeyStatus
    
    // COLD - используется редко
    Name        string
    Description string
    CreatedAt   time.Time
    Metadata    map[string]interface{}
    
    // HOT - обновляется каждый запрос
    Usage APIKeyUsage
}
```

#### ✅ ХОРОШО: Hot/Cold split
```go
// Hot path - только нужные данные
type APIKeyHot struct {
    ID             string       // 16 bytes
    Status         APIKeyStatus // 16 bytes
    ModelsAll      bool         // Fast check
    PermissionsAll bool
    IsExpired      bool
    _pad1          [5]byte      // Alignment
    
    Cold  *APIKeyCold      // Pointer to cold data
    Usage *APIKeyUsageHot  // Pointer to hot counters
    // Total: ~64 bytes (одна cache line)
}

// Cold path - редко используемые поля
type APIKeyCold struct {
    Name        string
    Description string
    KeyHash     string
    CreatedAt   time.Time
    Metadata    map[string]interface{}
    // ... остальные поля
}
```

### Структура для Concurrent Counters

**Шаблон для padded atomic counters:**

```go
type Counters struct {
    // Каждый счетчик в отдельной cache line
    RequestCount int64
    _pad1        [56]byte
    
    ErrorCount int64
    _pad2      [56]byte
    
    SuccessCount int64
    _pad3        [56]byte
}

func (c *Counters) IncrementRequests() {
    atomic.AddInt64(&c.RequestCount, 1)
}

func (c *Counters) IncrementErrors() {
    atomic.AddInt64(&c.ErrorCount, 1)
}

func (c *Counters) IncrementSuccess() {
    atomic.AddInt64(&c.SuccessCount, 1)
}

// Thread-safe snapshot
func (c *Counters) Snapshot() CountersSnapshot {
    return CountersSnapshot{
        Requests: atomic.LoadInt64(&c.RequestCount),
        Errors:   atomic.LoadInt64(&c.ErrorCount),
        Success:  atomic.LoadInt64(&c.SuccessCount),
    }
}

type CountersSnapshot struct {
    Requests int64
    Errors   int64
    Success  int64
}
```

### Чек-лист для новых структур данных

При создании новой структуры проверь:

- [ ] **Concurrent access?** → Используй atomic operations
- [ ] **Multiple atomic fields?** → Добавь padding между ними
- [ ] **Hot + Cold data mixed?** → Рассмотри hot/cold split
- [ ] **High update rate (>100/sec)?** → Обязательно padding
- [ ] **Global singleton?** → Padding acceptable (memory overhead minimal)
- [ ] **Many instances (>1000)?** → Взвесь memory vs performance trade-off
- [ ] **Тесты с `-race`?** → ОБЯЗАТЕЛЬНО для concurrent structures
- [ ] **Benchmarks?** → Докажи что оптимизация необходима

### Benchmarking Template

```go
func BenchmarkStructure_Sequential(b *testing.B) {
    s := NewStructure()
    
    b.ResetTimer()
    for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {
        s.Operation()
    }
}

func BenchmarkStructure_Parallel(b *testing.B) {
    s := NewStructure()
    
    b.RunParallel(func(pb *testing.PB) {
        for pb.Next() {
            s.Operation()
        }
    })
}

// Ожидаемый результат:
// Sequential: baseline
// Parallel (without padding): ~10x slower (false sharing)
// Parallel (with padding): ~same as sequential
```

### Memory Trade-offs

**Padding costs:**
- 1 padded int64: 64 bytes (vs 8 bytes) = **8x overhead**
- 4 padded counters: 256 bytes (vs 32 bytes) = **8x overhead**

**Приемлемо для:**
- ✅ Global singletons (Stats, Metrics) - overhead negligible
- ✅ Per-user/per-key counters если users < 10,000
- ✅ Any structure где performance gain > 3x

**НЕ приемлемо для:**
- ❌ Structures с миллионами instances (User records в БД)
- ❌ Редко используемые counters
- ❌ Read-only data

